$ DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.test:pw@aws-1-us-west-2.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres" pytest backend/tests/test_auth.py
REFUSING TO RUN PYTEST: DATABASE_URL points at production.

Tests write to public.profiles/conversations/messages and call
Supabase auth.admin.create_user. Running against prod corrupts
real customer data.

To run tests:
  unset DATABASE_URL
  export TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/wheellsverse_test
  pytest ...

Override (NOT recommended): PYTEST_ALLOW_PROD=1 pytest ...
